.TH KLIPR 1 "2026-08-20" "klipr 1.2.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
klipr \- clipboard history manager for the GTK4 desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B klipr
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Klipr
watches the system clipboard and records what is copied, both text and
images, so that an earlier entry can be pasted again later. The history is
searchable, entries can be pinned as favourites, and the program keeps
running in the system tray once its window is closed.
.PP
Running
.B klipr
while an instance is already running does not start a second copy: the
options below are handed to the running instance instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start without presenting the window. Klipr goes straight to the system tray
and begins recording. This is what the autostart entry uses.
.TP
.B \-t ", " \-\-toggle
Show the window if it is hidden, hide it if it is visible. This is the
command that the global keyboard shortcut is bound to.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a summary of the available options and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/klipr/clipboard.db
Clipboard history and favourites, stored as an SQLite database. The file is
not encrypted; it should be treated as carefully as any other file in the
home directory, because whatever has passed through the clipboard, including
passwords, may be in it.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/klipr/images/
Copied images, written as PNG files and de\-duplicated by content hash. A
file is removed once no history entry or favourite refers to it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/klipr/setting.json
User preferences: theme, history limit, close\-to\-tray, autostart and the
global shortcut. Created on first run from the packaged defaults in
.IR /usr/share/klipr/setting.json .
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/klipr.desktop
Autostart entry, written and removed by the autostart option in Klipr's own
settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/klipr/crash.log
Written only if Klipr terminates with an unhandled exception, and overwritten
by the next such failure. Honours
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME
when that is set.
.SH NOTES
.SS Display server
Klipr requests the X11 GDK backend. On a Wayland session it therefore runs
through XWayland rather than natively.
.SS System tray
The tray icon uses the StatusNotifierItem protocol, which needs a tray host
to be present. KDE Plasma, Xfce, Cinnamon and MATE provide one; on GNOME the
AppIndicator shell extension has to be installed and enabled. Without a tray
host the program still runs, and its window can be reached with
.B klipr \-\-toggle
or the global shortcut.
.SS Global shortcut
The shortcut is registered as a GNOME custom keybinding by running
.BR gsettings (1),
from
.BR libglib2.0-bin .
On desktops that do not use GNOME's keybinding settings, bind
.B klipr \-\-toggle
in the desktop's own keyboard configuration instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gsettings (1)
